{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (best: scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool at 0.650 acc), while image-only models are weak (best: ViT-L multiprofile at 0.332). Within RNA, scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 > scgpt, multiprofile > singleprofile, and avgpool > transformer. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether adding image features to the best RNA configuration provides any complementary signal or merely adds noise. This experiment (config_030: multimodal, scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) directly tests whether the simplest fusion (concat) of the best RNA setup with a modest image encoder improves over the 0.650 RNA-only baseline. It is the best next step because it extends the strongest known configuration along the single most important untested axis (fusion), uses the simplest fusion rule to isolate the effect of adding image information, and avoids changing multiple design choices simultaneously. If it fails to beat 0.650, it strongly argues against further multimodal exploration; if it succeeds, it justifies deeper fusion and image-encoder experiments."
}

